---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="DTP — AI Readiness Operating Loop"
  description="A DTP homepage concept focused on the operating loop from AI readiness signal to proof, MVP, pilot and adoption."
>
  <Header />
  <main class="concept operating-loop">
    <section class="loop-hero">
      <div class="loop-orb" aria-hidden="true"><span></span><span></span><span></span></div>
      <div class="ma-container loop-hero-grid">
        <div>
          <span class="ma-section-tag">// operating_loop.for_ai_value</span>
          <h1>Turn AI interest into decisions, proof and adoption.</h1>
          <p class="lead">DTP helps organisations move through the loop properly: understand the readiness signal, decide what matters, build the narrow proof, and keep the operating evidence visible.</p>
          <div class="ma-hero-actions"><a class="ma-btn ma-btn-mint" href="https://outlook.office.com/bookwithme/user/f0762b9af6a94ed2add9818a4f3ca4e5@digitaltechnologypartner.ai/meetingtype/qc2lOXjEdkO6GkMS_jZJrQ2?anonymous" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Book a Discovery Call</a><a class="ma-btn ma-btn-outline" href="#loop">Explore the loop →</a></div>
        </div>
        <div class="loop-device">
          <div class="device-header"><b>AI Readiness Loop</b><span>live operating picture</span></div>
          <div class="loop-map">
            <div class="node n1 active"><small>01</small>Listen</div><div class="node n2"><small>02</small>Diagnose</div><div class="node n3"><small>03</small>Decide</div><div class="node n4"><small>04</small>Build</div><div class="node n5"><small>05</small>Adopt</div>
          </div>
          <div class="device-footer"><span>next best action</span><strong>Prove the highest-confidence workflow.</strong></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ma-section intro-section">
      <div class="ma-container intro-grid">
        <div><span class="ma-section-tag">// why_this_matters</span><h2>AI is not a one-off project. It is an operating loop.</h2></div>
        <p>Useful AI work keeps moving between evidence, decision and implementation. The organisations that get value fastest are not the ones that run the most demos. They are the ones that can see what is happening, make better choices and test tightly.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="loop-section" id="loop">
      <div class="ma-container loop-cards">
        <article><span>01</span><h3>Listen</h3><p>Capture how people are already using AI, where pressure is building, and which work is ready for change.</p></article>
        <article><span>02</span><h3>Diagnose</h3><p>Separate enthusiasm from actual readiness across value, data, capability, governance and adoption.</p></article>
        <article><span>03</span><h3>Decide</h3><p>Give leadership a practical choice: encourage, control, investigate, stop or prove.</p></article>
        <article><span>04</span><h3>Build</h3><p>Where evidence supports it, deliver focused PoCs, MVPs, internal tools, workflow agents or pilots.</p></article>
        <article><span>05</span><h3>Adopt</h3><p>Track whether the work changes the process, improves decisions, and earns continued investment.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ma-section service-section">
      <div class="ma-container service-grid">
        <div class="service-copy"><span class="ma-section-tag">// offer_stack</span><h2>The loop is supported by four practical services.</h2><p>Each one can stand alone. Together they create a route from uncertain AI activity to useful operational proof.</p></div>
        <div class="service-list">
          <div><h3>AI Readiness Snapshot</h3><p>Low-friction signal for leaders who need to know whether there is enough substance to go deeper.</p></div>
          <div><h3>AI Readiness Diagnostic</h3><p>A structured look at adoption, appetite, risk, process opportunity, data and capability.</p></div>
          <div><h3>AI Readiness Advisory</h3><p>Interpretation and challenge so leadership can make the next decision rather than admire the data.</p></div>
          <div><h3>Focused AI Builds</h3><p>Focused builds where the diagnostic shows a worthwhile use case and an owner who can absorb it.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="evidence-section">
      <div class="ma-container evidence-grid">
        <div><span class="ma-section-tag">// evidence_not_hype</span><h2>What changes when the loop is working?</h2></div>
        <div class="evidence-board">
          <div><b>Visibility</b><p>Leadership knows where AI is already touching work.</p></div>
          <div><b>Prioritisation</b><p>The organisation stops treating every AI idea as equal.</p></div>
          <div><b>Control</b><p>Risk and governance become part of delivery, not an afterthought.</p></div>
          <div><b>Momentum</b><p>The best opportunities move quickly into small, useful proofs.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="ma-cta"><div class="ma-container ma-cta-inner"><h2>Build the AI loop before you build the next AI thing.</h2><p>If you know where the evidence is, the next build becomes much easier to justify.</p><a class="ma-btn ma-btn-mint ma-btn-lg" href="https://outlook.office.com/bookwithme/user/f0762b9af6a94ed2add9818a4f3ca4e5@digitaltechnologypartner.ai/meetingtype/qc2lOXjEdkO6GkMS_jZJrQ2?anonymous" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Book a Discovery Call</a></div></section>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  .operating-loop { background: var(--ma-bg); }

  /* Hero */
  .loop-hero { position: relative; overflow: hidden; padding: 10.5rem 0 6rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ma-border); }
  .loop-hero:before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: radial-gradient(circle at 68% 38%, rgba(0,229,160,.14), transparent 28%),
                radial-gradient(circle at 22% 70%, rgba(87,99,255,.12), transparent 34%);
  }

  /* Softer concentric rings — less busy */
  .loop-orb { position: absolute; right: 4vw; top: 7rem; width: 530px; height: 530px; border: 1px solid rgba(0,229,160,.14); border-radius: 50%; opacity: .42; }
  .loop-orb span { position: absolute; inset: 12%; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.05); border-radius: 50%; }
  .loop-orb span:nth-child(2) { inset: 28%; border-color: rgba(255,255,255,.04); }
  .loop-orb span:nth-child(3) { inset: 43%; background: rgba(0,229,160,.06); box-shadow: 0 0 60px rgba(0,229,160,.18); }

  .loop-hero-grid { position: relative; z-index: 2; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.02fr .98fr; gap: 4rem; align-items: center; }
  .loop-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 7vw, 6.6rem); line-height: .95; letter-spacing: -.065em; }
  .lead { font-size: 1.2rem; max-width: 650px; margin: 1.4rem 0 2.2rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,.8); }

  /* Loop device */
  .loop-device {
    background: linear-gradient(145deg, rgba(26,26,46,.88), rgba(10,10,15,.95));
    border: 1px solid var(--ma-border);
    border-radius: 24px;
    padding: 1.25rem;
    box-shadow: 0 28px 90px rgba(0,0,0,.44);
  }
  .device-header, .device-footer {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: center;
    border: 1px solid var(--ma-border);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 1rem;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,.03);
  }
  .device-header b, .device-footer strong { font-family: var(--ma-font-display); color: var(--ma-white); }
  .device-header span, .device-footer span { font-family: var(--ma-font-mono); font-size: .72rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,.52); }

  /* Loop map nodes */
  .loop-map { height: 380px; position: relative; margin: 1rem; border: 1px dashed rgba(0,229,160,.14); border-radius: 50%; }
  .loop-map:before { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 22%; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.08); border-radius: 50%; }
  .node {
    position: absolute;
    width: 112px;
    height: 112px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: rgba(26,26,46,.9);
    border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.14);
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    text-align: center;
    font-family: var(--ma-font-display);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.38);
  }
  .node small { display: block; font-family: var(--ma-font-mono); color: rgba(255,255,255,.45); font-size: .7rem; }
  .node.active {
    background: rgba(0,229,160,.1);
    border: 1px solid rgba(0,229,160,.5);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px rgba(0,229,160,.08), 0 4px 32px rgba(0,229,160,.2);
  }
  .node.active small { color: var(--ma-mint); }
  .n1 { top: 0; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%); }
  .n2 { top: 31%; right: 0; }
  .n3 { bottom: 0; right: 18%; }
  .n4 { bottom: 0; left: 18%; }
  .n5 { top: 31%; left: 0; }

  /* Intro section */
  .intro-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 3rem; }
  .intro-grid h2, .service-copy h2, .evidence-grid h2 { font-size: clamp(2.2rem, 4.8vw, 4.4rem); line-height: 1; }
  .intro-grid p { font-size: 1.18rem; color: rgba(255,255,255,.78); }

  /* Five-step loop cards — premium framework feel */
  .loop-section { padding: 1px 0; background: var(--ma-surface-alt); border-block: 1px solid var(--ma-border); }
  .loop-cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5,1fr); gap: 1px; background: var(--ma-border); padding: 0; }
  .loop-cards article { background: var(--ma-surface-alt); padding: 2.2rem 1.8rem; min-height: 280px; }
  .loop-cards span { font-family: var(--ma-font-mono); color: var(--ma-mint); font-size: .82rem; letter-spacing: .04em; }
  .loop-cards h3 { font-size: 1.6rem; margin: 3rem 0 .75rem; }
  .loop-cards p { color: rgba(255,255,255,.72); font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.6; }

  /* Service section */
  .service-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .8fr 1.2fr; gap: 4rem; }
  .service-copy p { color: rgba(255,255,255,.76); }
  .service-list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem; }
  .service-list div { background: var(--ma-surface); border: 1px solid var(--ma-border); border-radius: 14px; padding: 1.35rem; }
  .service-list h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-bottom: .5rem; }
  .service-list p { color: rgba(255,255,255,.72); font-size: .96rem; line-height: 1.55; }

  /* Evidence section — smoother transition, more breathing room */
  .evidence-section {
    padding: 8rem 0 7rem;
    background: #dff8ee;
    color: #0a0a0f;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(10,10,15,.1);
  }
  .evidence-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .75fr 1.25fr; gap: 4rem; }
  .evidence-grid h2 { color: #0a0a0f; }
  .evidence-board { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 1rem; }
  .evidence-board div { background: #f0fdf6; border: 1px solid rgba(10,10,15,.12); border-radius: 14px; padding: 1.35rem; }
  .evidence-board b { font-family: var(--ma-font-display); font-size: 1.35rem; }
  .evidence-board p { color: #2e4038; margin-top: .4rem; line-height: 1.55; }

  /* CTA breathing room */
  .operating-loop .ma-cta { padding: 7rem 0 8rem; }

  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .loop-hero-grid, .intro-grid, .service-grid, .evidence-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .loop-cards, .service-list, .evidence-board { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .loop-map { height: 460px; }
    .loop-orb { display: none; }
  }
</style>
